 @starstreamgamer3704  I know they have RAM reserved for the system, but it's more like 2.5GB that's unavailable. 12GB falls a bit short. And again, you'll probably want more VRAM than a console, due to usually worse PC optimisation (see Last of Us as an extreme example) and because, with a GPU twice as powerful as them, you will probably want to play games at higher resolutions (FFXVI is 720p at points on PS5 in 60hz mode) or maybe increase textures/RT effects -> more VRAM being used than on consoles.

As for VRAM usage, it's pretty similar. You don't really gain a significant advantage with either company. Back when AMD and Nvidia had similar levels of VRAM, it wasn't an issue, and the RX 7600 and RTX 4060 have almost identical performance whenever VRAM becomes an issue. 

Maybe you'll get some outliers when AMD optimisation is particularly bad, but it's usually similar usage. Some games will just use more VRAM if it's available to them, by loading up more things.

